/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (In this first part of our 7-Day DevOps Project, we will establish the essential Cloud Foundation and the Compute Layer for our application. The primary objective is to provision a reliable and secure deployment target by setting up a basic web application on an AWS EC2 instance.)
/E (In this first part of our 7-Day DevOps Project, we will establish the essential Cloud Foundation and the Compute Layer for our application. The primary objective is to provision a reliable and secure deployment target by setting up a basic web application on an AWS EC2 instance.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
endobj
174 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (This process involves crucial foundational steps: configuring the networking \(Security Groups\) to allow public HTTP access, and using a User Data Script to ensure the server infrastructure is correctly initialized with a basic web server. This validates that our future deployment target is fully operational from Day 1.)
/E (This process involves crucial foundational steps: configuring the networking \(Security Groups\) to allow public HTTP access, and using a User Data Script to ensure the server infrastructure is correctly initialized with a basic web server. This validates that our future deployment target is fully operational from Day 1.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Crucially, to enable automation and security, we will implement the necessary IAM roles \(following the principle of least privilege\) and associate them with our EC2 instance. This configuration allows the instance to securely communicate with the AWS CodeDeploy service, which is a non-negotiable prerequisite for building the robust CI/CD pipeline we will develop over the coming days.)
/E (Crucially, to enable automation and security, we will implement the necessary IAM roles \(following the principle of least privilege\) and associate them with our EC2 instance. This configuration allows the instance to securely communicate with the AWS CodeDeploy service, which is a non-negotiable prerequisite for building the robust CI/CD pipeline we will develop over the coming days.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
